  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "scenery-n",
      "view-n",
      "landscape-n"
    ],
    "note": "**Scenery** is the natural features of a whole area, seen as something to enjoy, and is uncountable: *the scenery in the mountains*. A **view** is what you can see from one particular place: *a view of the lake from our window*. A **landscape** is the land of an area seen as one whole, with its shape and features, and is countable: *a flat, empty landscape*."
  },
